	<item>
		<title>By: Craig Street</title>
		<link>http://drownedmadonna.com/13-underrated-madonna-songs/20141230#comment-12900</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Craig Street]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 02 Jan 2015 18:33:41 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://drownedmadonna.com/?p=3305#comment-12900</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[Excellent.  &quot;Love Profusion&quot; and &quot;Keep it Together&quot; instantly sprang to mind.  Madonna can write some amazing, catchy, and poignant songs (over and over and over).  It brings to mind what someone once said about Tracy Ullmann, BRILLIANT, when not left to her own devices.  I also cringed while listening to hear Hollywood and the aforementioned one.  My top choice for the list was &quot;Take a Bow&quot;; however, you may consider that well received! :)]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Excellent.  &quot;Love Profusion&quot; and &quot;Keep it Together&quot; instantly sprang to mind.  Madonna can write some amazing, catchy, and poignant songs (over and over and over).  It brings to mind what someone once said about Tracy Ullmann, BRILLIANT, when not left to her own devices.  I also cringed while listening to hear Hollywood and the aforementioned one.  My top choice for the list was &quot;Take a Bow&quot;; however, you may consider that well received! <img src="http://drownedmadonna.com/wp-includes/images/smilies/icon_smile.gif" alt=":)" class="wp-smiley" /></p>
]]></content:encoded>
	</item>
